From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:55:37 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] Input: synaptics-tcm: Keep the attention interrupt off across
 system sleep

The driver had no PM callbacks, so its attention interrupt stayed armed
through system suspend. On the Pixel 9a a touch while the system was
going down raised it after the SPI controller had suspended: the read
failed part way ("Attempted to sync while suspend"), every read after
that saw "bad message header a5 03 00 00", and the touchscreen stayed
dead after resume until the driver was rebound.

Disable the interrupt in suspend and enable it again in resume. A
report that arrives in between keeps the level-triggered line asserted
and is read once the interrupt is back on, with the bus already
resumed.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm.c
index 53ac4287a..1aa29458a 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm.c
@@ -831,6 +831,29 @@ static int tcm_probe(struct spi_device *spi)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Keep the attention interrupt off across system sleep: it can fire after
+ * the SPI controller has suspended, and a read then fails part way and
+ * leaves the message stream out of step.
+ */
+static int tcm_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct tcm_ts *ts = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	disable_irq(ts->spi->irq);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int tcm_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct tcm_ts *ts = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	enable_irq(ts->spi->irq);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(tcm_pm_ops, tcm_suspend, tcm_resume);
+
 static const struct of_device_id tcm_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "syna,s3908" },
 	{ }
@@ -847,6 +870,7 @@ static struct spi_driver tcm_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "synaptics-tcm",
 		.of_match_table = tcm_of_match,
+		.pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&tcm_pm_ops),
 	},
 	.id_table = tcm_spi_ids,
 	.probe = tcm_probe,
